---
import { Code } from "@astrojs/starlight/components";

import ArchitectureFlow from "../components/architecture-flow";
import ReferencePage from "../components/reference-page.astro";
import { architecture, architectureMermaid } from "../lib/architecture";
import { siteHref } from "../lib/reference";
---

<ReferencePage title="Architecture">
  <p class="command-help">Google supplies directory authority. The host reviews the plan and supplies credentials, policy and durable write budgets.</p>
  <ArchitectureFlow client:visible />
  <p class="command-help">Pan or use the zoom controls. Dashed nodes belong to the host.</p>
  <details>
    <summary>Data flow and source</summary>
    <ol>{architecture.nodes.map((node) => <li><a href={siteHref(`api/${node.module}/`)}>{node.label}</a> — {node.detail}.</li>)}</ol>
  </details>
  <h2>Read before writing</h2>
  <p>Audit stops at the plan. Live mode refreshes provider state, checks the reviewed hash, reserves the host's budget, applies one Slack profile and verifies it by reading it back. Replan for the next profile.</p>
  <p>Other provider workflows compose their own authority, lease and readback guards; this diagram follows <a href={siteHref("api/org-sync/service/")}>OrgSyncService</a>.</p>
  <details>
    <summary>Mermaid source</summary>
    <Code code={architectureMermaid()} lang="text" />
  </details>
  <p><a href={siteHref("architecture.mmd")} download>Download Mermaid</a></p>
</ReferencePage>
